  "_doc": "His medical books (#819; refs experiments/prop_lab/refs/doctor/): a shelf's row standing spine out (+z), 54 cm of them. The standard American texts a country doctor of 1882 owned: United States Dispensatory (Wood & Bache); National Dispensatory (Stille & Maisch); Therapeutics & Materia Medica (H. C. Wood); Medical Jurisprudence (Taylor); Fractures And Dislocations (Hamilton); Operative Surgery (S. Smith); Pathological Anatomy (Delafield); Midwifery (Playfair); Transactions Am. Med. Assoc. 1879 (a year's volume); Manual Of Chemistry (Fownes). Most in law sheep (tan sheepskin with a red and a black label lettered in gilt, the trade binding of medical books into the 1880s), some in publishers' cloth, a few in calf. Each book a member (wood `paper`: ~1.5 kg an octavo): it burns, a ball goes through it, the row comes down with its shelf. Drawn from glb:medical_books, every face printed on its own sheet (tools/blender/props/doctor_d3.py: Pillow, as the bottles' labels). Written by tools/props/doctor.py.",
